    crash_handler_and_fork_bridge_absent_from_seed_macos_2026-09-06, 1, "revalidated 2026-11-02 (close-invalid lane): validity=uncertain - cited source file still present and no evidence it stopped reproducing; keep open"
    crash_handler_and_fork_bridge_absent_from_seed_macos_2026-09-06, 2, "2026-11-09 status fix-implemented-verification-pending: both halves exist in C runtime (runtime.c crash handler, runtime_fork.c) and are verified natively on Darwin by src/runtime/test/rt_fork_crash_handler_selfcheck.c (15 checks, 0 failures, crash child rc=139); Darwin fork+null-write spec already in test/01_unit/lib/crash/crash_bundle_spec.spl (skip_on_interpreter). Pending: run that spec on an admitted self-hosted macOS binary."
    crash_handler_and_fork_bridge_absent_from_seed_macos_2026-09-06, 3, "2026-11-26 status fix-implemented-verification-pending: nm on manual-successor-v14/simple (macOS arm64 Stage-3) showed rt_fork_* present but rt_install_crash_handler absent because Core-C links runtime_native.c without runtime.c. Extracted shared crash handler to src/runtime/runtime_crash_handler_impl.h and wired into runtime_native.c (strong rt_install_crash_handler + spl_init_args call) and runtime.c (SPL_RUNTIME_NATIVE_TWIN). Added test/01_unit/runtime/rt_fork_crash_handler_darwin_test.shs (24/24 PASS on both Core-C strict link and legacy runtime.c). Compiled crash_bundle_spec.spl on a rebuilt Stage-4 macOS binary pending P4 qualification."

